[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=0.5,ystep=0.2] (0,0) grid (5,4.2);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.6,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {1/200,2/400,3/600,4/800} {\draw (-0.12,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,-0.12)--(\x,0); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.15) {$\x$};}
\draw[red,thick] (0,0)--(5,4);
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-2,2) {Interest (dollars)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2.5,-1) {Time (years)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (2.5,5.1) {Travel savings account};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph shows the simple interest earned on Priya's travel savings account. According to the graph, how much interest has been earned after $3$ years?

questions.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=0.5,ystep=0.2] (0,0) grid (5,4.2);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.6,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {1/200,2/400,3/600,4/800} {\draw (-0.12,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,-0.12)--(\x,0); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.15) {$\x$};}
\draw[red,thick] (0,0)--(5,4);
\draw[blue,dashed,<-] (0,2.4)--(3,2.4);
\draw[blue,dashed,<-] (3,0)--(3,2.4);
\fill[blue] (3,2.4) circle (2pt);
\node[font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (1.5,2.75) {$480$};
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-2,2) {Interest (dollars)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2.5,-1) {Time (years)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (2.5,5.1) {Travel savings account};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Read up from $3$ years to the line, then across to the interest axis.
$I = \$480.00$

